ibility is  let's turn to how we can use it as a  framework and what tools such as  automation  can impact inspiring credibility in  research  i propose automation has four supporting  pillars or ways for potentially  impacting research the first is  automation helps to generate  trustworthiness in research  it also offers reproducibility through  workflow optimization and  standardization  automation of workflows through  instrument processing protocols  and together  we significantly inspire confidence in  results  watch for the color-coded icons  throughout the remainder of the  presentation to highlight the potential  for automation's impact on research  let us define a few keywords that we  will be talking more about when we talk  about reproducibility  trustworthiness  is the credible transferable confirmable  and dependable  optimization is  operational efficiency and  standardization of procedure and  confidence is how sure you can be  of research  some current methods rely heavily on  manual processes that carry an inherent  risk for inter-operator process step  variability  handwriting identifiers on slides can  can be transposed or illegible  i might fit my slides for 32 seconds  while my co-worker might get faster or  smaller  my thigh might sit in hemotoxin for  three minutes while the next round might  sit for five minutes while the phone  rings  we may have all experienced some of  these examples in our daily lab length  and know it's these tiny hard to control  for nuances of manual process that can  significantly impact results  automation renews human variability  which optimizes your workflow and can  lead to credibility in your research  keeping the four pillars  of using automation to inspire  credibility in mind  i'm going to invite you to rethink some  of the current methods perhaps  and share a few tips and tricks about  how automation can impact research  remember how variable our examples of  manual tasks in the lab could be  automation low